Phase Theory predicts measurable effects:

10.1 Quantized Vortex Defect Persistence

Microfluidic vortices should exhibit stable topological phase cores.

10.2 Coherence-Bounded Turbulence

Energy spectra should reveal bounded defect clustering.

10.3 Phase Reconstruction

Optical flow interferometry may reconstruct hidden phase manifolds.

Potential tools could include systems from COMSOL and MIT research groups working in fluid visualization.

